      "description": "If ν and μ are Borel measures on ℝⁿ with μ the Lebesgue measure, then dν/dμ(x) = lim_{r→0} ν(B_r(x))/μ(B_r(x)) exists a.e. and equals the Radon-Nikodym derivative."
    },
    {
      "id": "s_total_variation_function",
